cleanup.description:
These {count} entries point to entities or areas that no longer exist in Home Assistant, usually after a device or integration was removed:

- Entity settings: {entities}
- Custom cards and popups: {cards}
- Area settings and area cards: {areas}
- Sensors below the area name, area graphs, weather and alarm entity: {settings}

{items}

Entities that are only disabled, unavailable or belong to an integration that is not loaded are **not** affected. Renamed entities take their settings along automatically and never show up here.

All touched files are copied to `dwains-dashboard/backups/` before anything is removed.

broken_configuration_files.description:
These files in `dwains-dashboard/configs/` are damaged or not valid YAML. The dashboard works without them until they are fixed or removed:

{files}

This message disappears once the files can be read again.
